# A pencil with one nilpotent Jordan block: the identity against N, where N
# shifts the basis one step and kills the last vector.
#
# The classical answer, and the one this fixture exists to hold: a pencil
# (I_n, J_n(lambda)) has rank n + 1, one more than its size, because the block
# is not diagonalisable and no change of coordinates makes it so. Here n = 3,
# so the rank is 4 and not 3. The pencil is regular, so it has no minimal
# indices at all and every term of the formula but the last two is zero.
field 2
shape 2 3 3

1 0 0
0 1 0
0 0 1

0 1 0
0 0 1
0 0 0
